<attribute name="changeDescription" nodeId="db445aa7">APR 2017 - updated role from Organizational Change Manager to Training Designer|MAR 2017 - updated purpose|APR 2016 - reworded brief description</attribute>
<attribute name="version" nodeId="50eefe9c"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="5d74bf97">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Gain buy-in to the timing and resourcing of onboarding and upskilling with the process workstreams. They will play
        in integral role in training.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Involve the business in testing the training side by side with the trainer in order to gain business support.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Monitor the upskilling of trainers to ensure that trainers are getting the support they need as well as critical
        feedback they should hear prior to attempting live training sessions.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="324c1d44"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="5f4d3ca9">Defining an effective trainer the trainer approach is critical to the roll out of training. &lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
A thorough train the trainer approach includes onboarding and upskilling tasks and timeline as well multiple opportunities
for the trainers to “test” the material, the system, the training environment, and their own training delivery. Ideally,
such testing is a precursor to running a training pilot.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="a03aff7c"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="b3cea5f7">To define an effective approach by which trainers will be brought on board, and upskilled to be able to deliver the
training.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="4afe069b"></attribute>
</Element>
